 ring world's base consisted of a strong  foundation material  which could not be worked it is  speculated early on that the creators of  the Ring world necessarily must have  possessed an easy method of elemental  transmutation in order to maintain  civilization the ring world had been  this ancient civilization solution to  the problem of overcrowding it was  equivalent in size to about 3 million  Earth's the ring world was a kind of  compromise between a Dyson Sphere and a  planet  the Explorers found the ring world to be  amazingly flat the Seas of the Ring  world were shallow the vegetation earth  Lake the ring world was also protected  by an automatic meteoroid defense system  to provide a day and night cycle  resembling an earth-like planet the ring  world was equipped with a secondary ring  of atmospheric shadow sweaters which  rotated providing the ring world with 30  hour days the construction of the ring  world remains a mystery throughout the  first two ring world novel it is assumed  that in order to build such a structure  a tremendous amount of energy and  resources would have been required and  the amount of time necessary to complete  the project would have no doubt in  several human lifespans by the time the  puppeteer is sent an expedition to the  ring world the civilization which had  built it had fallen the inhabitants had  devolved into many primitive societies  many of which had built mythologies  around the ones who had engineered the  ring world the ring world probably  couldn't exist in real life at least not  in the way it's described in Nivens  books it was pointed out by many years  ago that due to the fact that the  central mass of the ring world did not  move while the ring itself rotated that  the ring world could not maintain its  stability without additional thrusters  which could provide some kind of active  stabilization the ring world would have  been unstable the ring world series is  definitely a classic of the science  fiction